  "caption": "Quinn sat down, the office chair rolled away, and now every seat feels like a rock, especially when leaning back.\n\nYour tailbone takes more weight when you lean back or slump, and tight pelvic floor muscles can keep it grumbling.\n\nThings that often help: a wedge cushion with a cut-out to take pressure off, sitting tall on your sitting bones, breaking up long sitting spells, and gentle hip and back mobility before building strength. Warmth can help with comfort, and many cases settle over weeks to a few months.\n\nSee a doctor promptly after a big fall, or with saddle numbness, bladder or bowel changes, fever, unexplained weight loss, or pain that keeps getting worse.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
